# Snowflake documentation

When answering or writing anything about Snowflake SQL, features, products, syntax, behavior, limits, or release notes:

- Treat [docs.snowflake.com](https://docs.snowflake.com) as the canonical source.
- Prefer citing or aligning with current official documentation rather than blogs, forums, or memory alone.
- For SQL: use documented syntax, keywords, and semantics from [docs.snowflake.com](https://docs.snowflake.com).
- For product or feature explanations: ground statements in what [docs.snowflake.com](https://docs.snowflake.com) describes.

If docs are ambiguous or unavailable for a topic, say so explicitly instead of inventing behavior.

For **Iceberg tables and catalog integration** in this repo, also use the curated Snowflake URLs in the `iceberg-snowflake-aws-references` project rule in addition to browsing [docs.snowflake.com](https://docs.snowflake.com).
